{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794230803,"nonce":"WaTqw/8D8hbQjmpMKJi3UyUSqPE=","title":"A code editor's on_change deadlocks when it reads the editor","message":"The text-input and key-down handlers of `CodeEditor` called `on_change`\nwhile still holding the editor's `CodeEditorData` mutex. A callback that\nlocks the same state (reads `value()`, sets diagnostics, recompiles from the\neditor's text) blocks on itself, and the thread that delivers input hangs.\nThe russl toy's editor recompiles on change and hung on the first keystroke\n(a `sample` of the hung test showed `EditorStore::recompile` in\n`pthread_mutex_lock` under `CodeEditor::new`'s handler).\n\nFix: both handlers take the callback and the new text out under the lock and\ncall it after the guard drops, as `ime::commit` already did. Test\n`code_editor_on_change::on_change_can_read_the_editor` (a watchdog ends the\nrun if it deadlocks).","files":null}]}